 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 507547,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Which expression equals 10<span data-math=\"x\">x</span>?<br>\n<span data-math=\"\\left( {8x + 12x} \\right) \\div 4x-2x \">\\left( {8x + 12x} \\right) \\div 4x-2x </span>\n<br>\n<span data-math=\"8x + (12x \\div 4x)-2x \">8x + (12x \\div 4x)-2x </span>\n<br>\n<span data-math=\"8x + 12x \\div \\left( {4x - 2x} \\right)\"> 8x + 12x \\div \\left( {4x - 2x} \\right)</span>\n<br>\n<span data-math=\"(8x + 12x) \\div \\left( {4x - 2x} \\right)\"> (8x + 12x) \\div \\left( {4x - 2x} \\right)</span>\n",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<table class=\"unnumbered unstyled\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"\\left( {8x + 12} \\right) \\div 4x - 2x\"></span></td>\n<td>Divide the first two terms by 4<i>x</i>.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"\\left( {8x \\div 4x} \\right) + \\left( {12 \\div 4x} \\right) - 2x\"></span></td>\n<td>Simplify.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"2 + 3x - 2x\"></span></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>Like terms are constants or have the same variable and exponent. Add the coefficients and keep the same variable.</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered unstyled\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"2 + x\"></span></td>\n<td>This is not equal to 10<i>x.</i> Try again.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"8x + \\left( {12 \\div 4x} \\right) - 2x\"></span></td>\n<td>Divide 12 by 4<i>x</i>.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"8x + \\left( {3x} \\right) - 2x\"></span></td>\n<td>Combine the like terms.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"9x\"></span></td>\n<td>This is not equal to 10. Try again.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"8x + 12x \\div \\left( {4x - 2x} \\right)\"></span></td>\n<td>Subtract inside the parentheses.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"8x + 12x \\div \\left( {2x} \\right)\"></span></td>\n<td>Divide by 2<i>x</i>.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"8x + 6\"></span></td>\n<td>This is not equal to 10. Try again.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"\\left( {8x + 12x} \\right) \\div \\left( {4x - 2x} \\right)\"></span></td>\n<td>Do the operations inside the parentheses.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"\\left( {20x} \\right) \\div \\left( {2x} \\right)\"></span></td>\n<td>Divide.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>10</td>\n<td>This is equal to 10.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>The expression <span data-math=\"\\left( {8x + 12x} \\right) \\div \\left( {4x - 2x} \\right)\"></span> equals 10.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"(8x + 12x) \\div \\left( {4x - 2x} \\right)\">(8x + 12x) \\div \\left( {4x - 2x} \\right)</span>"
    }
